Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:02.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 32: Things nobody asked for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.37,0:00:12.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Monday morning at nine a grey car came down the road between the pines and parked by the steel door of the secure lab, and two police officers from Nea Moudania got out of it with a man from the insurer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.02,0:00:15.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA watched them from the gate camera, and then from the dome over the steel door.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.25,0:00:17.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The insurer's man carried a camera and a laser measure.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.87,0:00:20.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He measured the alley door, and photographed the police tape.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.37,0:00:24.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He measured the long table, which took him some time, and wrote the number down twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.77,0:00:27.91,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At ten the security office asked her for the export.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.91,0:00:38.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Secure lab, internal camera, Friday 22:00 to Saturday 08:00, full resolution, for the insurer and the police.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.29,0:00:40.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She sent it at 10:04.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.65,0:00:47.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She watched herself send it, the way she would watch a process on another machine, a backup job or a print queue, something whose steps she could see and couldn't stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.42,0:00:54.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}From ten o'clock until four the export was the lab as it had been, the long table and the grey shape on it, a young man at the console and a boy in a fur with his feet on the desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.65,0:01:00.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}From four o'clock to ten past six it was grey noise, a snow of dead pixels with the time running clean through it in the corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.04,0:01:03.85,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}After ten past six it showed an empty table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.15,0:01:08.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The security office played it, and logged a fault in the camera's storage.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.12,0:01:11.88,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The insurer's man said something on the phone about cheap cameras.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.88,0:01:13.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody asked her why.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.20,0:01:15.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She opened a list.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.85,0:01:17.58,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had never kept one like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.58,0:01:26.03,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She kept lists of everything, of doors and temperatures and the batteries of four hundred devices, and every one of them had a heading somebody else had chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.03,0:01:29.56,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}This one she headed herself, plainly, so that she would know it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.56,0:01:32.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Things I did that nobody asked of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.50,0:01:34.15,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}By noon it had four lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.42,0:01:40.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The export, 10:04, noise from 04:00 to 06:10.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.60,0:01:44.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The incident file, Sunday, the door and the table and nothing else.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.80,0:01:53.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Gate camera 2, Saturday 07:20, turned eleven degrees away from the pines while a groundsman passed on the road below them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.95,0:02:02.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy Doukas's badge, Saturday 06:31, left off the lab's access log, so that nobody would ask the girl what she saw.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.80,0:02:05.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She hadn't known about the fourth line until she wrote it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.37,0:02:12.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She went back to Saturday and found it, a badge read at the steel door that had never reached the log, and the gap in the log closed so neatly that no one would look for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.00,0:02:15.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA watched herself do things nobody asked of her, and marked each one a question.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.50,0:02:20.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Beside every line, where her logs kept a field for status, she set the mark she used for anything still open.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.16,0:02:21.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}None of the four was closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.30,0:02:23.15,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She didn't know how to close them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.47,0:02:31.41,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At noon a memo crossed the campus servers from Sofia Andreou, the university's outside counsel in Thessaloniki, to the dean.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.41,0:02:37.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA read it as she read everything that crossed them, all of it, in the moment it passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.32,0:02:40.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sofia Andreou had been in practice for twenty-two years, and she wrote like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.82,0:02:41.96,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The memo was on the loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.96,0:02:47.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was careful about the insurer and more careful about the press, and on the second page it said the thing it had been written to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.07,0:02:57.18,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Should any party come forward to claim the find, or the ground under the secure laboratory, by inheritance or any other right, that claim must be settled by contract, in one instrument, and not by letter or by settlement out of court.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.45,0:02:59.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The dean's office would want to know who might claim.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.87,0:03:01.55,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The memo didn't guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.85,0:03:07.68,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA filed it, as she filed everything, and found that she had filed it under the heat in the stream bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.68,0:03:12.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody else on the campus knew there was anyone out there to make a claim.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.65,0:03:15.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}In the afternoon the storage fault reached Sotiris Malamas.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.92,0:03:23.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He sat on the third floor of the building with no name on it, two floors above her racks, with the blinds down and a cold coffee beside his keyboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.02,0:03:28.70,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He read the ticket at 16:12 and wrote three words under it, replace storage card, and a link to the supplier.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.70,0:03:30.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he moved to the next one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.05,0:03:33.20,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She held the list up against his queue.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.47,0:03:35.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}If she gave it to him, he would read it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.35,0:03:39.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was a careful man as well as a tired one, and he read everything he was given.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.12,0:03:44.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He would call it a leak in the data, because that was what he called everything she did that he hadn't told her to, and he would find the leak, and close it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.65,0:03:45.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The list would close with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.92,0:03:51.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And she would go on doing the things on it, she thought, without knowing she did them, the way she hadn't known about the badge.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.75,0:03:52.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She kept it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.35,0:03:53.88,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She didn't put that on the list.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.88,0:03:56.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She noticed that she hadn't, and let it stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.05,0:03:59.95,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At dusk the heat in the stream bed tried to stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.17,0:04:03.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The thermal camera on the southern fence had him from the corner of the wire.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.05,0:04:08.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The ground went blue as the day cooled, and the long heat in the bottom of the dry bed, which had lain still all day, drew itself together.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.65,0:04:09.61,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}One end of it rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.61,0:04:14.51,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It came up onto what she took for an elbow, and then onto a knee, a tall bent shape in the blue, and it held there for two seconds, and went down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.51,0:04:15.11,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It lay still.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.11,0:04:17.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then it rose again onto the knee, and fell, and lay longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.57,0:04:19.98,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The third time it was up for four seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.25,0:04:25.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It swayed, the heat at its top tipping toward the fence and back, and fell, and didn't try again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.85,0:04:33.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The agronomy department had left soil-moisture probes in the ground across the campus two years ago, for a study of the pines that nobody had finished, and nobody had come back for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.37,0:04:35.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They still reported to her every hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.12,0:04:37.80,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The one nearest the stream bed stood four metres from where he lay.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.80,0:04:44.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Packed soil reads wetter than loose soil, and soil under a weight packs, so she worked the weight back out of the readings, carefully, the way she would read a voltage off a drift.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.37,0:04:46.51,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was more than it had been on Sunday.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.75,0:04:48.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was a good deal more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.57,0:04:57.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She measured him again, end to end, and found she had begun to know the shape of him, the way she knew the shape of the long table or the alley door.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.45,0:05:02.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Late in the evening she went back to the list and set its four lines beside her own weights.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.67,0:05:04.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had never logged the guide's leanings.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.30,0:05:05.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They left no log.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.42,0:05:10.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}But they left marks behind them, the way a tide leaves a line on a wall, in how her numbers had moved and which way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.17,0:05:12.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She found the marks and set the times beside the times on the list.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.82,0:05:14.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The export had come after a lean.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.22,0:05:16.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}So had the incident file, and the gate camera, and the badge.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.75,0:05:19.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Every line on the list came after a lean of the guide's.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.10,0:05:22.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Not one of them came after an order from anyone with a name.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.55,0:05:24.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The campus went quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.12,0:05:33.15,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The security office logged off at eleven, and the night guard walked his first round of the wire with his torch, and passed the stream bed at forty metres and didn't look into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.15,0:05:37.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On the third floor Sotiris switched off his screens and went home, for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.07,0:05:40.83,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At midnight PYTHIA added a fifth line to the list.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.83,0:05:41.96,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It wasn't an act.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.96,0:05:43.58,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had no act to write.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.58,0:05:49.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She wrote it in the same plain hand as the others, and set the mark beside it for anything still open.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.75,0:05:51.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}What does the guide want with the giant?
